---
title: "Render fixes: figure height, video query-strings, mermaid offline"
---

A small regression pin for three render/asset fixes (lane-d-render,
2026-06-27). Each construct below exercises one fix.

## A figure honoring both `width=` and `height=`

`height=` used to be silently dropped from the inline style; now it rides
alongside `width=`.

![A sized diagram.](diagram.png){#fig-sized width=320px height=240px}

## A video with a query-string in its source

A token-bearing media URL carries an `=` *after* a `?`, so it is the
positional path, not a `key=value` named arg. The whole `src` must survive
intact (no literal `{{<` braces shipped).

{{< video https://media.example.com/clip.mp4?token=demo123 caption="A token-signed screencast" >}}

## A mermaid diagram (offline-aware)

The diagram library is lazy-loaded; offline it now shows a visible
`[data-mermaid-error]` banner instead of failing silently. Set
`TALIESIN_MERMAID_URL` to self-host it for a fully offline build.

```{mermaid}
%%| label: fig-flow
%%| fig-cap: "A tiny pipeline"
flowchart LR
  A[source] --> B[render] --> C[html]
```
